  "blocks": [
    {
      "file_id": "f6f4a7b83ac743fd8b42e369c7aca904",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "block_id": "7405f2ead527e2076feaee33bb24eafb1550f9e5f381655bd90f5997d1ec781d",
      "text": "Table S1 presents calculated { T _ { c } } \\mathbf { s } of \\mathrm { L a H _ { n } }   ( n = 4 ,   8 , and 10) and \\mathrm { Y H _ { 1 0 } } at high pressures for different models and parameters. It is seen that the McMillan and Eliashberg equations lead to similar results for small λ. For larger λ, however, the Eliashberg equation predicts higher Tc values. Table S2 contains the lattice parameters and atomic coordinates for the predicted structures."
    },
    {
      "file_id": "f6f4a7b83ac743fd8b42e369c7aca904",
      "pdf_page": 1,
      "block_id": "302dc447428183eea11eef3571bd94f49ebfe2b47a7a69af6866ae8f9a28019d",
      "text": "We compare the calculated density of states (DOS) for \\mathrm { L a H _ { 1 0 } , } \\mathbf { Y H } _ { 1 0 } , and \\mathbf { \\bar { S } H } _ { 3 } in Fig. S3. In the case of \\mathrm { S H } _ { 3 , } we found a DOS at the Fermi level of 7.1 states/Ry which is close to the value of 6.93 states/Ry found in the previous work (42). The calculated N ( E _ { f } ) of \\mathrm { L a \\dot { H } _ { 1 0 } } and \\mathrm { Y H _ { 1 0 } } at 250 GPa is larger than that of \\mathrm { S H } _ { 3 }"
    },
    {
      "file_id": "f6f4a7b83ac743fd8b42e369c7aca904",
      "pdf_page": 5,
      "block_id": "77ff781672e778fb1f9cab92ea6df797b6f9413694b0749d33deb01230b32b9d",
      "text": "Table S1. T _ { c } of La-H and Y-H systems at different pressures calculated using the McMillan and Eliashberg equations"
    },
